{"title":"2021 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/8/83870118206bd0e612b5c9e3def2ef95460e368b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be an integer. Find all positive real solutions to the following system of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f93f5c51ea4b04b4992b003b39479f29018f6bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> equations:<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/1/301cd0ead59d39f1135e7e94925f2eeda12023c4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} a_{1} &amp;=\\frac{1}{a_{2 n}}+\\frac{1}{a_{2}}, &amp; a_{2}&amp;=a_{1}+a_{3}, \\\\ a_{3}&amp;=\\frac{1}{a_{2}}+\\frac{1}{a_{4}}, &amp; a_{4}&amp;=a_{3}+a_{5}, \\\\ a_{5}&amp;=\\frac{1}{a_{4}}+\\frac{1}{a_{6}}, &amp; a_{6}&amp;=a_{5}+a_{7}, \\\\ &amp;\\vdots \\\\ a_{2 n-1}&amp;=\\frac{1}{a_{2 n-2}}+\\frac{1}{a_{2 n}}, &amp; a_{2 n}&amp;=a_{2 n-1}+a_{1} \\end{align*}\" width=\"357\" height=\"217\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For any odd <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27ebff36e5fe7b73c01169464d28534241ef7a58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n = \\frac{1}{a_{n-1}} + \\frac{1}{a_{n+1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"146\" height=\"42\" />. Additionally, for any even <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/1/131e8e6b3244ce8f2d6da57fb0672fc31d61e762.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_m = a_{m-1} + a_{m+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"149\" height=\"16\" />. Substituting gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/e/9fef58e7f845d787d3179edbf4ac2c088f64a700.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_m = \\frac{2}{a_m} + \\frac{1}{a_{m-2}} + \\frac{1}{a_{m+2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"205\" height=\"42\" />, other than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/3/6f3eaf8047a3f5bebfc5c43e27123a15a44d7540.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=2$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/6/bd6c2b6035a39aaeac72c692b7b878b2a060cc03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=2n$\" width=\"59\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Consider the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6bdec4394870e8a713538ce428bea9d41c8775f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/0/d609644351b090d52a832e380991b3104592fb4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2k} = b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"17\" />. Then, say out of the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/3/7133a5fd2b8a97d6c4273d0d0f8b86d5787ff8aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[b_1, b_2, \\cdots, b_n]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"111\" height=\"20\" /> let the maximum value of an element in the set be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and the minimum value be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/5/585d7c5c4b1872608d63e64d59fe7beb77587855.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\le X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Then, we also know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/c/46c1551414313a9bf7c275f2716d278dccc6d256.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k = \\frac{2}{b_k} + \\frac{1}{b_{k-1}} + \\frac{1}{b_{k+1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"180\" height=\"42\" />, plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6bdec4394870e8a713538ce428bea9d41c8775f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bba0e96a79a7fd5a40591c2b679ff76fdbffc41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{2}{x} + \\frac{1}{b_{k-1}} + \\frac{1}{b_{k+1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"169\" height=\"42\" />.\n</p><p>We know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/9/e49011a44ef479d6d28a52d75085a62977a25a9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{b_k} \\ge \\frac{1}{X}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"67\" height=\"41\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/8/ea88769321fe9a9d8dc385dafa692fd653271e6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\ge \\frac{2}{x} + \\frac{2}{X}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"94\" height=\"38\" />. Similarly, plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and using an inequality gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/c/6fcd61622e902373e87cc0a373d1d2abfd40f84c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{x} + \\frac{2}{X} \\ge X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"100\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/8592026b5e874289d9e806f214123b3321ea1587.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\ge \\frac{2}{x} + \\frac{2}{X} \\ge X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"134\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/4/c94df167b0a757c98d19913d91fb7b927265b77a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\ge X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />. We also showed earlier that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/5/585d7c5c4b1872608d63e64d59fe7beb77587855.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\le X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/4/cf4a0177d26e8414817020bb2911640104496de5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" />. So, all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/56331f2f2110a9332540a65efa78eed8abe2a049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"10\" /> are constants and equal to each other. \n</p><p>Now, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/3/cc38e32ae48c0c2373beb6647d1dd9a462e93ba7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2k-1}=w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/5/6252fe9be0e23478369924257d7d7baf9a4195ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2k}=z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/d/40df2dab4a8a58babf54f8be965c7cc18c116833.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w = \\frac{2}{z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"53\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/4/1b422ccf46e060222770130eb85cbc7a6c675f3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=2w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" />. Solving gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/a/eba745a0810833511d924977fc74208fcbb37fd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"45\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/6/5e6dc42bb0d892a136cd56c48b13585b42428825.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=2$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>~pl246631\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO\" title=\"2021 USAJMO\">2021 USAJMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO_Problems\" title=\"2021 USAJMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=176&amp;year=2021\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2021 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2021 USAJMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2021 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2021 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2021 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAJMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAJMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAJMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018020242\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.033 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.057 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 215/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1294/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 54/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6703/5000